  "summary": "Trump's approve % (not net) on the Silver Bulletin CSV 'approve' column was 38.97% on July 24, 2026, range-bound at 38.3–40.1% over the prior two months. With a ~21-day horizon to August 14 and a heavily-smoothed, slow-moving series, I ran a Monte Carlo (sigma_21=0.85 + 12% news-shock component + mild reversion to band center 39.2), yielding a center of 39.03, P10=37.86, P90=40.20. The distribution is slightly wider than the observed band to allow for possible news shocks. The question bounds (33.95–46.05) sit far in the tails.",
  "reasoning": "My forecast for Donald Trump's approval rating (approve %) on the Silver Bulletin tracker for August 14, 2026:\n\n**Median: 39.0%** (P10: 37.9%, P90: 40.2%)\n\n**Key reasoning:**\n- The question resolves on the **\"approve\" column of the CSV** — the raw approval percentage (~39%), NOT the net approval headline (-17). This distinction was critical.\n- Current value: **38.97%** (July 24, 2026 CSV), range-bound at 38.3–40.1% over the past two months.\n- With only a ~21-day horizon and a heavily-smoothed, slow-moving polling average, large swings are unlikely. My Monte Carlo added a modest news-shock component and mild mean-reversion, producing a distribution slightly wider than the observed 2-month band.\n- The question bounds (33.95–46.05) sit far in the tails — essentially all probability mass falls comfortably inside.",
